WEBVTT

00:00:07.670 --> 00:00:10.360
What'd you want to talk about, Hotshot?

00:00:11.260 --> 00:00:13.450
You must've noticed, too.

00:00:14.110 --> 00:00:15.610
It's about that.

00:00:17.070 --> 00:00:22.970
Since Makishima-san left and Tadokoro-san 
and Kinjou-san stopped coming to practice,

00:00:22.970 --> 00:00:26.420
we've started practicing with 
just Teshima-san and Aoyagi-san.

00:00:27.210 --> 00:00:30.530
You must feel it, too. Keenly.

00:00:31.460 --> 00:00:33.800
The huge size of the hole 
left by the third-years.

00:00:41.170 --> 00:00:42.560
Not really.

00:00:42.560 --> 00:00:45.170
It's not Teshima-san and Aoyagi-san's fault.

00:00:45.170 --> 00:00:48.620
They've gotten more than strong enough.

00:00:48.620 --> 00:00:50.870
But the reality is our 
practices have gotten weaker

00:00:50.870 --> 00:00:53.400
than when the third-years were around.

00:00:54.270 --> 00:00:57.480
We experienced it firsthand 
at this year's Inter-High.

00:00:57.910 --> 00:01:01.740
Its fierceness, its level, its brutality.

00:01:01.740 --> 00:01:02.910
At this rate...

00:01:04.520 --> 00:01:06.540
We can't win next year.

00:01:07.410 --> 00:01:09.250
Not even a single stage.

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:14.300
<b>Tadokoro Jin</b>

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:14.300
<b>Imaizumi Shunsuke</b>

00:01:10.440 --> 00:01:14.300
Even the sprint and mountain tags
could fall out of our reach.

00:01:19.560 --> 00:01:21.900
What are we supposed to do, then?

00:01:21.900 --> 00:01:23.680
All we can do is practice.

00:01:23.680 --> 00:01:24.730
Naruko...

00:01:25.400 --> 00:01:28.100
You should become an all-rounder like me.

00:01:29.490 --> 00:01:30.940
Abandon the sprint.

00:01:30.940 --> 00:01:33.940
Hotshot, who do you think you're talking to?

00:01:33.940 --> 00:01:37.740
Cry all you want, but the 
third-years aren't coming back.

00:01:37.740 --> 00:01:39.200
We have to change.

00:01:39.200 --> 00:01:43.690
Are you stupid? I'm the Speedman 
of Naniwa, Naruko Shoukichi!

00:01:43.690 --> 00:01:48.000
Our team doesn't have enough riders who 
can aim for the finish line right now.

00:01:48.470 --> 00:01:51.580
Road racing is a race to 
reach the finish line.

00:01:53.530 --> 00:01:56.410
If you start working on it now, 
you'll be ready by the Inter-High.

00:01:56.410 --> 00:01:57.180
What?

00:01:57.180 --> 00:02:00.300
Spend less time practicing 
on flats and climb.

00:02:00.300 --> 00:02:02.680
You need to change your style completely.

00:02:05.150 --> 00:02:06.570
I can't do that.

00:02:06.570 --> 00:02:08.450
No way. I refuse.

00:02:08.450 --> 00:02:11.770
Besides, we're classmates.
I don't take orders from you.

00:02:12.310 --> 00:02:14.970
It's for the team. It's so we can win.

00:02:14.970 --> 00:02:19.030
You already showed a glimpse 
of that at the Inter-High.

00:02:19.570 --> 00:02:21.830
You climbed despite being a sprinter.

00:02:21.830 --> 00:02:23.650
That's not something a normal rider can do.

00:02:24.160 --> 00:02:26.630
You can climb. You have 
the right feel for it.

00:02:26.630 --> 00:02:27.980
Your body is light, too.

00:02:27.980 --> 00:02:30.770
You already have a keen nose for the goal.

00:02:30.770 --> 00:02:31.920
Do it.

00:02:35.270 --> 00:02:36.300
I can't.

00:02:36.710 --> 00:02:40.490
I can't let the quiet one pass me now.

00:02:40.490 --> 00:02:41.760
Sorry, Hotshot.

00:02:42.230 --> 00:02:45.030
I'm a pure sprinter.

00:02:46.240 --> 00:02:51.400
<b>Sohoku
High
School
Bicycle
Racing
 Club</b>

00:02:48.120 --> 00:02:52.610
<i>RIDE.05 A Different Kind of Race!!</i>

00:02:53.210 --> 00:02:55.150
I'm nervous.

00:02:55.150 --> 00:02:58.610
I know. I'll use this to relax.

00:03:00.370 --> 00:03:02.490
Okay, I'm ready.

00:03:02.490 --> 00:03:03.910
Ready, and...

00:03:03.910 --> 00:03:05.670
Thanks for the food!

00:03:10.110 --> 00:03:12.000
We had an unexpected visitor.

00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:14.510
A local middle school student 
came to watch us practice.

00:03:14.510 --> 00:03:18.110
He didn't realize the door was locked 
and pulled as hard as he could.

00:03:18.540 --> 00:03:19.510
Rice Boy...

00:03:21.770 --> 00:03:25.980
You're the one who broke 
our legendary club's door?

00:03:25.980 --> 00:03:27.740
Teru-chan, I'm here.

00:03:28.430 --> 00:03:29.800
He's huge!

00:03:29.800 --> 00:03:31.380
Sadatoki!

00:03:31.380 --> 00:03:32.100
What?

00:03:32.100 --> 00:03:34.770
You know him, Sugimoto?

00:03:34.770 --> 00:03:38.390
Yes. Can you introduce yourself, Sadatoki?

00:03:38.390 --> 00:03:40.030
Yeah, Teru-chan.

00:03:40.350 --> 00:03:43.110
I'm studying to get into Sohoku!

00:03:43.110 --> 00:03:46.580
If I pass the exam, I hope 
to join the bicycle club!

00:03:46.580 --> 00:03:48.730
My name is Sugimoto Sadatoki!

00:03:49.770 --> 00:03:50.870
Sugimoto?

00:03:51.260 --> 00:03:54.210
My dream is to race with 
my brother Teru-chan!

00:03:54.550 --> 00:03:57.630
Y-You're Sugimoto-kun's younger brother?

00:03:57.630 --> 00:03:58.460
One, two.

00:03:58.460 --> 00:04:01.670
One, two. One, two.

00:04:01.670 --> 00:04:03.930
Go, Sadatoki!

00:04:03.930 --> 00:04:05.890
Go, go!

00:04:05.890 --> 00:04:08.350
Strong, isn't he?

00:04:08.350 --> 00:04:10.410
Th-That's amazing.

00:04:10.410 --> 00:04:12.690
Um, are you Onoda-san?

00:04:12.690 --> 00:04:13.190
Yes.

00:04:13.950 --> 00:04:17.130
My brother's told me all about you.

00:04:17.130 --> 00:04:19.070
I'm a huge fan of yours.

00:04:19.070 --> 00:04:20.900
Huh? What?!

00:04:21.240 --> 00:04:25.660
Onoda-san, you're small.
Far smaller than I imagined.

00:04:25.660 --> 00:04:28.150
But you're strong. You're so cool.

00:04:28.150 --> 00:04:30.290
Oh, I'm not...

00:04:30.290 --> 00:04:34.540
If I get accepted by Sohoku 
and get into the bicycle club,

00:04:34.540 --> 00:04:37.380
I want to become an 
incredible rider like you.

00:04:40.820 --> 00:04:42.880
Yeah, g-good luck.

00:04:42.880 --> 00:04:44.150
Thank you!

00:04:45.260 --> 00:04:48.420
I can't believe you have someone 
who wants to join the club already.

00:04:48.420 --> 00:04:50.870
The bicycle club's all set.

00:04:51.560 --> 00:04:52.850
Miki?

00:04:53.490 --> 00:04:56.250
Sorry, yeah. You're right.

00:04:57.190 --> 00:05:00.060
Shall we get practice started, then?

00:05:00.060 --> 00:05:02.610
We're training on Minegayama 
today, right, Teshima-san?

00:05:02.610 --> 00:05:05.740
Sadatoki's been wanting 
to ride with you, Onoda.

00:05:05.740 --> 00:05:06.450
What?

00:05:06.990 --> 00:05:08.700
I'm against it.

00:05:10.030 --> 00:05:11.970
I've been listening.

00:05:11.970 --> 00:05:14.080
Hey, big boy. Ride this.

00:05:15.250 --> 00:05:17.710
A th-three-drum roller?

00:05:18.020 --> 00:05:22.840
It's a test. If you can't ride this,
I won't let you participate in our practice.

00:05:22.840 --> 00:05:24.050
You can't be serious.

00:05:24.050 --> 00:05:26.130
Sadatoki's never rode one before.

00:05:26.540 --> 00:05:31.180
Every day of practice counts 
for us. We're desperate.

00:05:31.680 --> 00:05:34.810
We can't give you special treatment 
just because you're someone's brother.

00:05:35.140 --> 00:05:36.780
You have only one chance.

00:05:36.780 --> 00:05:38.230
If you fail, leave.

00:05:38.230 --> 00:05:39.820
Imaizumi-kun.

00:05:39.820 --> 00:05:42.630
But it's hard to balance 
on three-drum rollers...

00:05:42.630 --> 00:05:44.740
At least give him a few chances.

00:05:47.170 --> 00:05:50.240
<i>Can he succeed with only one chance?</i>

00:05:50.760 --> 00:05:54.240
<i>In road racing, that's an important factor.</i>

00:05:55.260 --> 00:05:57.260
<i>Onoda did it.</i>

00:06:08.340 --> 00:06:09.340
Huh.

00:06:09.340 --> 00:06:12.730
Well, that was easy.

00:06:12.730 --> 00:06:18.020
We can afford to take him to 
one practice to see how he does.

00:06:18.020 --> 00:06:19.270
Yes, sir.

00:06:19.270 --> 00:06:22.310
So, how good is he on a bike?

00:06:22.640 --> 00:06:25.560
You mean Sadatoki? He's fine.

00:06:25.560 --> 00:06:31.120
After all, I've taught him everything 
I know about road racing.

00:06:34.680 --> 00:06:35.330
He's so slow.

00:06:35.330 --> 00:06:40.000
He's strong enough to lift a mommy bike,
but he's a slow sprinter.

00:06:40.000 --> 00:06:41.670
Maybe it's his form.

00:06:42.100 --> 00:06:45.480
His form is awful. It's just like Sugimoto's.

00:06:45.480 --> 00:06:46.670
It's inefficient.

00:06:47.210 --> 00:06:50.820
He may have been good enough to ride on 
the roller, but he's no good on a bike.

00:06:50.820 --> 00:06:52.590
Wait, Imaizumi-kun.

00:06:53.070 --> 00:06:56.810
Sadatoki-kun's strength could be climbing.

00:06:59.540 --> 00:07:00.690
Looks like you were wrong.

00:07:01.100 --> 00:07:02.910
It's another exact copy.

00:07:04.700 --> 00:07:06.450
Sadatoki-kun, you can do it.

00:07:06.450 --> 00:07:10.360
I mean, when you're climbing, uh...

00:07:10.360 --> 00:07:12.780
Yes, sir. What am I supposed to do?

00:07:13.270 --> 00:07:14.820
He's wasting his time.

00:07:14.820 --> 00:07:16.500
Let's go, Teshima-san.

00:07:17.700 --> 00:07:22.790
If there's anything he's specialized at, 
it's being in perfect sync with his brother.

00:07:23.180 --> 00:07:24.750
Let's go.

00:07:25.340 --> 00:07:26.630
Synchronization?

00:07:29.300 --> 00:07:31.760
<i>Maybe this is how they felt.</i>

00:07:32.760 --> 00:07:35.890
<i>As younger members join the team,</i>

00:07:35.890 --> 00:07:42.600
<i>you pray for just a handful 
you can use at the Inter-High.</i>

00:07:43.250 --> 00:07:46.920
<i>Then your intentions just might reach them.</i>

00:07:46.920 --> 00:07:50.860
<i>It's a crushing, almost wishful feeling.</i>

00:07:52.020 --> 00:07:57.800
<i>Is that how you felt, Kinjou-san, 
Tadokoro-san, Makishima-san?</i>

00:07:58.940 --> 00:08:02.230
<i>I guess I had hoped for more.</i>

00:08:02.230 --> 00:08:05.080
<i>Honestly, I'm disappointed 
by our current situation.</i>

00:08:06.440 --> 00:08:07.540
Let's go, Onoda.

00:08:08.210 --> 00:08:10.210
Unfortunately, we have to leave them behind.

00:08:10.650 --> 00:08:12.630
We don't have any more time for them.

00:08:12.950 --> 00:08:13.880
What?

00:08:13.880 --> 00:08:16.970
We have things we have to do today.

00:08:17.380 --> 00:08:20.060
We're facing the entire country.

00:08:26.340 --> 00:08:27.780
Thanks for the food.

00:08:27.780 --> 00:08:30.830
No, wait. I mean thank you.

00:08:30.830 --> 00:08:34.490
I had fun riding with you, Onoda-san.

00:08:34.840 --> 00:08:38.490
It's okay. I'll ride with Sadatoki.

00:08:40.660 --> 00:08:42.910
Sorry I couldn't do anything for you.

00:08:49.080 --> 00:08:51.540
Imaizumi, do you have some time to spare?

00:08:51.540 --> 00:08:53.740
Maybe about three minutes.

00:08:53.740 --> 00:08:54.970
Teshima-san?

00:08:54.970 --> 00:08:57.960
Go ride with Rice Boy for three minutes.

00:08:58.900 --> 00:09:01.370
No, thank you. We've already 
reached a conclusion.

00:09:01.370 --> 00:09:02.100
Are you sure?

00:09:03.560 --> 00:09:07.710
Unlike his brother, he's big and powerful.

00:09:07.710 --> 00:09:10.400
He even had a good enough sense 
of balance to ride on the roller.

00:09:10.400 --> 00:09:13.880
But he was slow on a bike. Why?

00:09:13.880 --> 00:09:18.160
Because of his form.
He's copying his brother's form.

00:09:18.690 --> 00:09:21.530
Sugimoto's form makes him lose power.

00:09:21.530 --> 00:09:24.990
Without power, you get left 
behind in road racing.

00:09:24.990 --> 00:09:26.750
That's why he always falls behind.

00:09:27.150 --> 00:09:29.330
Then what if his form were improved?

00:09:29.330 --> 00:09:33.510
Then... No, it can't be fixed that quickly.

00:09:33.510 --> 00:09:35.470
At the very least, not in three minutes.

00:09:35.470 --> 00:09:39.090
Are you sure? Couldn't you do it?

00:09:39.470 --> 00:09:44.100
You said he had the power to synchronize.

00:09:44.620 --> 00:09:48.060
Go test it out. It means he has potential.

00:09:48.760 --> 00:09:50.400
<i>Potential?</i>

00:09:50.780 --> 00:09:56.360
Imaizumi, isn't that how
 you brought Team Sohoku...

00:09:56.950 --> 00:10:00.740
its top-class ace climber?

00:10:01.150 --> 00:10:02.200
<i>Onoda...</i>

00:10:06.190 --> 00:10:08.210
Huh? Imaizumi-kun?

00:10:08.540 --> 00:10:09.790
Imaizumi-san?

00:10:10.180 --> 00:10:12.810
Big boy, you get one chance.

00:10:12.810 --> 00:10:16.210
Forget everything your brother 
taught you about road racing.

00:10:16.760 --> 00:10:18.140
What are you talking about?

00:10:20.020 --> 00:10:25.770
Copy that small bespectacled guy's form 
and do your best to catch up to him.

00:10:27.320 --> 00:10:29.960
My idol Onoda-san's form?

00:10:30.770 --> 00:10:36.200
He should be able to handle that.
Sadatoki's a fast learner.

00:10:36.200 --> 00:10:39.420
And Sadatoki's watched videos 
of the first-year race

00:10:39.420 --> 00:10:41.950
and our training camp over and over.

00:10:43.320 --> 00:10:44.790
<i>Onoda-san's...</i>

00:10:45.220 --> 00:10:46.370
<i>Onoda-san...</i>

00:10:46.370 --> 00:10:49.160
<i>The pressure changed. Is he...</i>

00:10:49.160 --> 00:10:50.540
Onoda-san!

00:10:54.340 --> 00:10:55.300
Onoda-san!

00:10:57.720 --> 00:10:59.350
H-How?

00:11:00.500 --> 00:11:02.180
I-I caught up.

00:11:04.820 --> 00:11:05.890
Sadatoki-kun!

00:11:06.210 --> 00:11:08.300
Are you okay, Sadatoki?

00:11:08.820 --> 00:11:12.400
<i>It was only for a moment,
but he copied his form perfectly.</i>

00:11:12.760 --> 00:11:15.560
<i>He succeeded twice with only 
a single chance each time.</i>

00:11:16.290 --> 00:11:19.150
<i>Was it a coincidence? If it wasn't, then...</i>

00:11:19.650 --> 00:11:21.710
Thanks for the food, Onoda-san.

00:11:21.710 --> 00:11:23.080
Oh, it's fine.

00:11:22.030 --> 00:11:24.490
Thanks for the food.

00:11:23.080 --> 00:11:25.000
No, really. Thank you.

00:11:25.540 --> 00:11:26.460
Thank you.

00:11:26.460 --> 00:11:28.720
Smile, Imaizumi.

00:11:28.720 --> 00:11:31.620
You're supposed to praise your 
juniors when they do well.

00:11:35.160 --> 00:11:36.340
Thanks for the food.

00:11:35.630 --> 00:11:37.770
Really, it's okay.

00:11:37.770 --> 00:11:38.670
Rice Boy.

00:11:39.560 --> 00:11:40.340
Yes?

00:11:41.870 --> 00:11:43.840
G-Good job.

00:11:44.990 --> 00:11:46.760
Imaizumi-kun, what's wrong with you?

00:11:46.760 --> 00:11:49.620
I-Imaizumi is making a conflicted face!

00:11:49.620 --> 00:11:53.850
I can't do it. I don't 
compliment people often.

00:11:54.520 --> 00:11:56.310
Thanks for the food.

00:11:56.310 --> 00:11:59.300
Uh, I...

00:12:05.130 --> 00:12:07.160
Thanks for staying late.

00:12:07.590 --> 00:12:10.200
What did you want to talk about?

00:12:10.540 --> 00:12:14.090
Could I take time off 
practice over the holiday?

00:12:15.500 --> 00:12:20.670
I'm having doubts about what's right 
for me and the path I should take.

00:12:21.160 --> 00:12:24.890
I'm sorry. It's only a possibility, but...

00:12:26.030 --> 00:12:29.060
Could I quit being a sprinter?

00:12:34.650 --> 00:12:36.900
Quit being a sprinter?

00:12:37.420 --> 00:12:42.980
It's only a maybe. I'm just 
saying it's a possibility.

00:12:43.410 --> 00:12:48.280
That's alarming. It affects our team.

00:12:48.940 --> 00:12:53.120
Tadokoro-san passed on the role 
of sprinter to you.

00:12:53.120 --> 00:12:55.230
Your abilities leave nothing to be desired.

00:12:55.230 --> 00:12:56.670
What is there to worry about?

00:13:00.380 --> 00:13:03.590
I'm sorry! Please don't ask, 
just give me the three days off!

00:13:03.970 --> 00:13:06.490
I'm thinking of going home to Osaka.

00:13:06.490 --> 00:13:09.420
I want to return to where 
I started and think things over.

00:13:09.420 --> 00:13:11.620
I want to find my own answer.

00:13:13.100 --> 00:13:14.760
You're not too smart, are you?

00:13:15.850 --> 00:13:17.550
You've been too stubborn

00:13:17.550 --> 00:13:20.760
to ask Tadokoro-san about whatever's 
bothering you, haven't you?

00:13:22.020 --> 00:13:22.730
I...

00:13:23.090 --> 00:13:27.090
It means it's too heavy a 
concern to discuss with others.

00:13:27.090 --> 00:13:29.120
Naruko, that sounds just like you.

00:13:30.060 --> 00:13:32.610
You can go until you're satisfied.

00:13:34.050 --> 00:13:38.120
I'm back to the city where 
I was born and raised, Osaka!

00:13:38.120 --> 00:13:40.500
<b>Naruko Snacks</b>

00:13:43.000 --> 00:13:45.510
<b>Naruko Shoukichi-kun
Congratulations on your team's victory!
Celebrating a triumphant return!!</b>

00:13:54.190 --> 00:13:57.590
<i>I guess I'll go to where it all started.</i>

00:14:03.790 --> 00:14:06.340
<i>I might be able to find something here.</i>

00:14:08.520 --> 00:14:11.870
This brings back memories. 
It's been six months.

00:14:12.200 --> 00:14:14.370
That sign's the finish line.

00:14:15.880 --> 00:14:21.130
The fastest guys in Osaka gather here.

00:14:23.020 --> 00:14:26.630
I learned to sprint by racing here every day.

00:14:28.970 --> 00:14:31.220
They're so cool.

00:14:31.550 --> 00:14:33.720
This is where I first 
encountered road racing!

00:14:34.190 --> 00:14:36.180
My home course!

00:14:36.670 --> 00:14:39.350
This is where everything started!

00:14:39.350 --> 00:14:44.150
One lap is 600 meters of 250-meter
straights and one turn.

00:14:44.760 --> 00:14:47.290
Fighting against and 
utilizing the sea breeze,

00:14:47.290 --> 00:14:51.110
I used tricks, instinct, and 
technique to seize victory!

00:14:51.110 --> 00:14:51.990
He's fast!

00:14:51.990 --> 00:14:54.100
His cornering and speed are incredible!

00:14:54.730 --> 00:14:55.620
That jersey...

00:14:56.020 --> 00:14:57.730
That's Chiba's Sohoku!

00:14:57.730 --> 00:15:00.000
What? You mean this year's 
Inter-High winners?

00:15:00.000 --> 00:15:05.060
I heard a red-headed sprinter 
from Osaka joined Chiba's Sohoku.

00:15:05.060 --> 00:15:08.120
The sprinter Naruko Shoukichi!

00:15:08.870 --> 00:15:10.300
<i>Sprinter...</i>

00:15:11.130 --> 00:15:14.660
<i>Fast, flashy, and speeding 
through corners at top speed.</i>

00:15:14.660 --> 00:15:17.140
<i>Racing past the scenery 
faster than everyone else.</i>

00:15:17.140 --> 00:15:20.770
<i>A world of glorious make-or-break contests.</i>

00:15:21.140 --> 00:15:22.880
<i>That's what it means to be a sprinter!</i>

00:15:22.880 --> 00:15:27.950
<i>It's the world I admired! The path I believed in!</i>

00:15:27.950 --> 00:15:30.780
<i>I can't abandon this that easily.</i>

00:15:30.780 --> 00:15:33.380
<i>My red blood is screaming for it!</i>

00:15:34.120 --> 00:15:37.490
Let's race, Sohoku.
How does three laps sound?

00:15:39.090 --> 00:15:44.140
I'm Handai High School's sprinter,
Kakimoto Ryudai.

00:15:44.140 --> 00:15:46.530
They call me the Dragon 
of Rokko's Winter Winds.

00:15:46.530 --> 00:15:48.380
I'm undefeated on this course.

00:15:50.070 --> 00:15:51.930
Bring it on. Let's do three laps.

00:15:52.490 --> 00:15:56.640
<i>If I fail here, I'll have failed 
as a sprinter. I'll give it up.</i>

00:15:56.640 --> 00:15:59.180
Ready, go!

00:15:59.180 --> 00:16:00.680
You won't beat me!

00:16:02.140 --> 00:16:05.360
<i>The answer can always be found in battle.</i>

00:16:05.360 --> 00:16:06.230
First lap!

00:16:06.230 --> 00:16:10.570
It's a race between the red-haired Sohoku 
rider Naruko and Handai High's Kakimoto!

00:16:10.570 --> 00:16:15.350
<i>It seems like it's true this Kakimoto 
guy is undefeated on this course.</i>

00:16:15.350 --> 00:16:17.370
<i>He's keeping up with me.</i>

00:16:17.370 --> 00:16:19.700
Third lap! One lap left!

00:16:21.260 --> 00:16:25.980
Sohoku's Naruko, your sprinting 
and cornering are incredible.

00:16:25.980 --> 00:16:27.870
It's no wonder you won nationals.

00:16:27.870 --> 00:16:34.510
But this is an unofficial race. 
Anything goes on this different kind of track.

00:16:35.290 --> 00:16:41.850
I'll show you why they really call me the 
Night Dragon of Rokko's Winter Winds.

00:16:42.770 --> 00:16:43.800
There it is!

00:16:43.800 --> 00:16:46.270
The Night Dragon Kakimoto special!

00:16:47.150 --> 00:16:49.800
Surprised? Of course you are.

00:16:49.800 --> 00:16:53.280
Not only am I fast, but I glow!

00:16:53.280 --> 00:16:59.450
Like a nightscape of Kobe seen from
Mt. Rokko, I'm worth a million dollars.

00:16:59.450 --> 00:17:02.270
Why Kobe when I'm from Osaka? 
They're close enough.

00:17:02.270 --> 00:17:04.080
Don't worry about the details.

00:17:05.970 --> 00:17:07.380
That's so cool!

00:17:08.470 --> 00:17:11.840
Now it's full speed ahead! 
It's a straight line to the finish line!

00:17:11.840 --> 00:17:14.620
<i>Oh, whoops. Calm down.</i>

00:17:14.620 --> 00:17:15.870
<i>I'm in the middle of the race.</i>

00:17:15.870 --> 00:17:17.350
<i>This is no time to be admiring his bike.</i>

00:17:17.350 --> 00:17:18.640
Naruko's fallen behind!

00:17:18.640 --> 00:17:20.800
<i>No matter the circumstances, I'll win.</i>

00:17:20.800 --> 00:17:23.060
<i>I learned this feeling during the Inter-High.</i>

00:17:25.070 --> 00:17:27.600
Move, idiot! The flashiest man here...

00:17:31.900 --> 00:17:36.530
is me, Naruko Shoukichi! Yeah!

00:17:36.530 --> 00:17:38.100
What was that? Amazing!

00:17:38.100 --> 00:17:40.270
He stretched so far ahead 
before the finish line!

00:17:40.270 --> 00:17:43.200
That's how the champions, Sohoku, sprint!

00:17:45.240 --> 00:17:48.080
If I beat you, I'll be top-class.

00:17:48.080 --> 00:17:50.960
Sohoku's Naruko, I'm your next opponent.

00:17:52.070 --> 00:17:53.550
It's been a while.

00:17:54.340 --> 00:17:58.650
I'm Nara Sanri Academy's white-hot 
sprinter, Daitsubu Takeshi.

00:17:58.650 --> 00:18:00.470
I'll only turn the other cheek thrice.

00:18:00.840 --> 00:18:03.100
<i>Who the hell is he?</i>

00:18:03.590 --> 00:18:05.790
This is my bike.

00:18:06.520 --> 00:18:07.840
That's...

00:18:07.840 --> 00:18:12.220
They're popular in Europe. It's a track bike.

00:18:12.220 --> 00:18:13.630
Even the gears have been removed.

00:18:13.630 --> 00:18:15.630
It's light. It's strong.

00:18:15.630 --> 00:18:19.610
It's a bike made exclusively 
for riding flats.

00:18:19.920 --> 00:18:21.240
The hollowed out tube...

00:18:21.240 --> 00:18:24.120
The super-light handles 
made for track racing...

00:18:24.500 --> 00:18:26.080
Do you know what happens

00:18:26.080 --> 00:18:31.130
when I combine them with my barrel-like legs,
which were made for sprinting?

00:18:31.640 --> 00:18:37.050
In scientific reactions, when you combine 
pure reagents, you get miraculous results.

00:18:37.710 --> 00:18:41.470
Come, Sohoku sprinter! It's a three-lap race!

00:18:42.140 --> 00:18:44.140
I'll only turn the other cheek thrice!

00:18:44.490 --> 00:18:45.600
Is that your catchphrase?

00:18:45.910 --> 00:18:50.100
<i>Jeez, these freaks keep 
coming one after another.</i>

00:18:50.560 --> 00:18:54.900
<i>But I can tell they all love bikes.</i>

00:18:54.900 --> 00:18:56.400
<i>I'm the same way.</i>

00:18:56.970 --> 00:18:59.990
<i>So I'll sprint as hard as I can.</i>

00:18:59.990 --> 00:19:03.290
<i>I think he said something about purity.</i>

00:19:03.290 --> 00:19:10.120
<i>Sorry, but Naruko Shoukichi is a 
natural-born 100 percent pure sprinter!</i>

00:19:12.610 --> 00:19:14.380
You're pretty fast.

00:19:14.740 --> 00:19:18.800
I'm just unthinkably fast.

00:19:18.800 --> 00:19:21.740
I excel at straight lines 
as I ride with flair!

00:19:21.740 --> 00:19:24.350
I'm the prodigal speedster!

00:19:30.740 --> 00:19:34.070
<i>Uh-oh, I've gotten stronger.</i>

00:19:34.070 --> 00:19:37.410
<i>I'm faster than I was 
when I used to ride here.</i>

00:19:37.410 --> 00:19:41.360
<i>I can tell I'm using my muscles,
and my speed's on a whole different level.</i>

00:19:42.460 --> 00:19:45.580
<i>Did riding in the Inter-High make me grow?</i>

00:19:46.280 --> 00:19:49.250
<i>Was it my friendly rivalry with 
the old man and Aoyagi-san?</i>

00:19:49.810 --> 00:19:54.290
<i>Sorry, hotshot. I can't give up this gift.</i>

00:19:54.670 --> 00:20:00.670
<i>My next race will be my last one.
If I win, I'll keep riding as a sprinter.</i>

00:20:03.010 --> 00:20:05.240
Shall we race?

00:20:06.890 --> 00:20:11.140
<i>M-Midousuji? Kyoto Fushimi's ace?</i>

00:20:11.140 --> 00:20:16.650
Isn't that Midousuji, who won the first day's 
race and two number tags on the second?

00:20:16.650 --> 00:20:23.070
He beat Hakone Academy's ace 
sprinter, #4 Shinkai, in a sprint!

00:20:23.070 --> 00:20:27.140
I came to Osaka since I was bored

00:20:27.140 --> 00:20:31.370
and heard a gross freak in 
a yellow jersey was here.

00:20:31.370 --> 00:20:35.400
Thanks for the compliment.
Does that mean you came to see me?

00:20:35.400 --> 00:20:37.040
Thank you.

00:20:37.040 --> 00:20:40.050
<i>My last opponent is him of all people?</i>

00:20:42.310 --> 00:20:44.300
<i>It's just another race.</i>

00:20:44.710 --> 00:20:51.140
Since it's a 600-meter track, how does 
a ten-lap, six-kilometer race sound?

00:20:51.140 --> 00:20:53.940
Sure. It's my last race.

00:20:53.940 --> 00:20:55.350
Give me everything you've got.

00:20:55.350 --> 00:20:59.700
It's your last race. Make sure 
you squeeze out every last drop.

00:21:01.170 --> 00:21:05.440
But it wouldn't be fun to just race.

00:21:05.440 --> 00:21:10.620
Why don't we each bet something important?

00:21:16.290 --> 00:21:21.550
Sure. I'd already decided for myself,
no matter who I was racing...

00:21:22.380 --> 00:21:25.880
If I win the next race,
I'll keep riding as a sprinter.

00:21:26.650 --> 00:21:27.550
If I lose...

00:21:29.050 --> 00:21:30.970
I'll quit sprinting!

00:23:08.670 --> 00:23:10.700
Imaizumi, you dropped something.

00:23:11.860 --> 00:23:13.700
<b>Love Hime
The Three-Hour Extra-Dimensional Labyrinth</b>

00:23:12.380 --> 00:23:13.700
Huh?

00:23:14.060 --> 00:23:15.310
Uh, that's...

00:23:15.310 --> 00:23:20.040
Oh, don't worry. I don't have any 
problem with this kind of thing.

00:23:20.040 --> 00:23:23.240
As a kid, I used to watch this stuff 
all the time with my brother.

00:23:23.240 --> 00:23:25.630
I'm an experienced anime watcher.

00:23:26.410 --> 00:23:28.850
Well, we all have our own tastes.

00:23:28.850 --> 00:23:29.760
It's not that!

00:23:31.270 --> 00:23:33.260
Imaizumi-kun, good morning.

00:23:33.260 --> 00:23:34.730
The other day when we went to <i>Love Hime</i>—

00:23:34.730 --> 00:23:36.020
Not right now!

00:23:36.330 --> 00:23:39.980
<i>NEXT RIDE Naruko VS Midousuji</i>

00:23:39.980 --> 00:23:44.980
This is a work of fiction. All characters and organizations
 appearing in this work are fictional. In this work,
 characters sometimes engage in dangerous activities.
 While riding bicycles on actual roads,
 please follow all traffic laws and ride safely.
